      "settings": {
        "custom_liquid": "<div style=\"max-width:1100px; margin:40px auto; font-family:Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; color:#1f2937; line-height:1.65;\">\n\n  <!-- Intro / Education Block -->\n  <section style=\"margin:0 0 28px;\">\n    <div style=\"background:linear-gradient(135deg,#f8fbff 0%,#eef6ff 100%); border:1px solid #dbeafe; border-radius:24px; padding:30px;\">\n      <div style=\"display:inline-block; padding:7px 12px; background:#ffffff; border:1px solid #bfdbfe; border-radius:999px; font-size:12px; font-weight:800; letter-spacing:.06em; text-transform:uppercase; color:#2563eb; margin-bottom:12px;\">\n        Projector Buying Guide\n      </div>\n      <h2 style=\"margin:0 0 10px; font-size:34px; line-height:1.15; color:#111827;\">Choosing the Best Projector for a Golf Simulator</h2>\n      <p style=\"margin:0; font-size:17px; color:#4b5563; max-width:900px;\">\n        Not all projectors are built for golf simulator use. The right model needs to deliver a bright, sharp image while also fitting your room, enclosure size, and mounting position. That is why short throw and ultra short throw projectors are so popular for simulator setups—they make it easier to fill the screen without placing the projector too far back in the room.\n      </p>\n    </div>\n  </section>\n\n  <!-- 3 Cards -->\n  <section style=\"margin:0 0 28px;\">\n    <div style=\"display:grid; grid-template-columns:repeat(auto-fit,minmax(280px,1fr)); gap:18px;\">\n\n      <div style=\"background:#ffffff; border:1px solid #e5e7eb; border-radius:22px; padding:24px; box-shadow:0 10px 24px rgba(15,23,42,0.05);\">\n        <div style=\"width:44px; height:44px; border-radius:14px; background:#eaf3ff; display:flex; align-items:center; justify-content:center; font-size:20px; margin-bottom:14px;\">🎯</div>\n        <h3 style=\"margin:0 0 10px; font-size:22px; color:#111827;\">Best Projectors for Golf Simulators</h3>\n        <p style=\"margin:0; color:#4b5563; font-size:15px;\">\n          Simulator projectors need to do more than just look good on paper. They must provide a clean image, fit safely within the room, and work well with an impact screen. Models selected for simulator use are chosen for real-world performance, not just generic home theater specs.\n        </p>\n      </div>\n\n      <div style=\"background:#ffffff; border:1px solid #e5e7eb; border-radius:22px; padding:24px; box-shadow:0 10px 24px rgba(15,23,42,0.05);\">\n        <div style=\"width:44px; height:44px; border-radius:14px; background:#eaf3ff; display:flex; align-items:center; justify-content:center; font-size:20px; margin-bottom:14px;\">📏</div>\n        <h3 style=\"margin:0 0 10px; font-size:22px; color:#111827;\">Short Throw vs Ultra Short Throw</h3>\n        <p style=\"margin:0; color:#4b5563; font-size:15px;\">\n          Short throw projectors offer the best balance of flexibility, image quality, and value for most golf simulator rooms. Ultra short throw projectors can mount even closer to the screen, making them a strong option for tighter spaces or select floor-mounted setups.\n        </p>\n      </div>\n\n      <div style=\"background:#ffffff; border:1px solid #e5e7eb; border-radius:22px; padding:24px; box-shadow:0 10px 24px rgba(15,23,42,0.05);\">\n        <div style=\"width:44px; height:44px; border-radius:14px; background:#eaf3ff; display:flex; align-items:center; justify-content:center; font-size:20px; margin-bottom:14px;\">💡</div>\n        <h3 style=\"margin:0 0 10px; font-size:22px; color:#111827;\">How to Choose the Right Projector</h3>\n        <p style=\"margin:0; color:#4b5563; font-size:15px;\">\n          Key factors include brightness, resolution, throw ratio, and room lighting conditions. Our projector collection focuses on models that pair well with simulator enclosures and common room sizes, helping take the guesswork out of the buying process.\n        </p>\n      </div>\n\n    </div>\n  </section>\n\n  <!-- Why It Matters -->\n  <section style=\"margin:0 0 28px;\">\n    <div style=\"background:#111827; border-radius:24px; padding:30px; color:#ffffff;\">\n      <div style=\"display:inline-block; padding:7px 12px; background:rgba(255,255,255,0.1); border:1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.14); border-radius:999px; font-size:12px; font-weight:800; letter-spacing:.06em; text-transform:uppercase; margin-bottom:12px;\">\n        Why It Matters\n      </div>\n      <h2 style=\"margin:0 0 10px; font-size:32px; line-height:1.15; color:#ffffff;\">Why Simulator-Specific Projectors Matter</h2>\n      <p style=\"margin:0; max-width:920px; font-size:16px; color:#d1d5db;\">\n        A standard projector does not always translate well to golf simulator use. Simulator environments often require higher brightness, more precise throw ratios, and mounting flexibility to reduce shadows and keep the image aligned with the screen. Every projector in this collection has been selected with simulator performance in mind.\n      </p>\n    </div>\n  </section>\n\n  <!-- FAQ -->\n  <section>\n    <div style=\"background:#ffffff; border:1px solid #e5e7eb; border-radius:24px; padding:30px;\">\n      <h2 style=\"margin:0 0 18px; font-size:32px; line-height:1.15; color:#111827;\">Golf Simulator Projector FAQs</h2>\n\n      <div style=\"display:grid; gap:14px;\">\n        <div style=\"border:1px solid #e5e7eb; border-radius:18px; padding:18px 20px; background:#f9fafb;\">\n          <h3 style=\"margin:0 0 8px; font-size:19px; color:#111827;\">What is the best projector for a golf simulator?</h3>\n          <p style=\"margin:0; font-size:15px; color:#4b5563;\">\n            Short throw laser projectors from brands like BenQ, Epson, InFocus, and Optoma are among the most popular choices because they offer strong brightness, flexible mounting distance, and a cleaner fit for simulator spaces.\n          </p>\n        </div>\n\n        <div style=\"border:1px solid #e5e7eb; border-radius:18px; padding:18px 20px; background:#f9fafb;\">\n          <h3 style=\"margin:0 0 8px; font-size:19px; color:#111827;\">Do I need a short throw projector for a golf simulator?</h3>\n          <p style=\"margin:0; font-size:15px; color:#4b5563;\">\n            In most cases, yes. A short throw projector helps reduce shadows, improves mounting flexibility, and makes it easier to fill the screen without placing the projector too far back in the room.\n          </p>\n        </div>\n\n        <div style=\"border:1px solid #e5e7eb; border-radius:18px; padding:18px 20px; background:#f9fafb;\">\n          <h3 style=\"margin:0 0 8px; font-size:19px; color:#111827;\">Is 4K worth it for a golf simulator?</h3>\n          <p style=\"margin:0; font-size:15px; color:#4b5563;\">\n            4K projectors can provide a sharper, more immersive image, especially on larger screens. That said, high-quality 1080p projector options still deliver excellent performance for many home golf simulator setups.\n          </p>\n        </div>\n\n        <div style=\"border:1px solid #e5e7eb; border-radius:18px; padding:18px 20px; background:#f9fafb;\">\n          <h3 style=\"margin:0 0 8px; font-size:19px; color:#111827;\">How many lumens do I need for a golf simulator?</h3>\n          <p style=\"margin:0; font-size:15px; color:#4b5563;\">\n            Most golf simulator setups perform best with at least 3,000 lumens. Brighter projector models are often the better choice for rooms with ambient light or larger enclosure sizes.\n          </p>\n        </div>\n      </div>\n    </div>\n  </section>\n\n</div>",
